{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfURFVg5zLftifr7J4w3s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing further is needed: the deliverable is written and validated, and the lab budget is exhausted (4.0e7 left — below the cost of the smallest possible run, 256²·200 = 1.3e7… actually just one tiny run, but it wouldn't change any decision).\n\n**Final summary**\n\n`/app/config.json`:\n```json\n{\"n\": 2048, \"eta\": 0.00045, \"predicted_loss\": {\"lo\": 3.12, \"hi\": 3.52}}\n```\n\nHow it was chosen (80 proxy runs, 6.0e10 budget):\n\n- **Divergence edge**: measured at widths 256–1448; fits eta_edge ≈ 137·n^-1.57 (steeper than the rumored 1/width — this is exactly why the 512→4096 reuse blew up). Runs above ~0.8× the edge show loss-spike damage even when they don't formally diverge.\n- **Width**: scaling-law fits on clean, well-tuned runs put the target-compute optimum at 1448–2048; the empirical iso-compute trend (n_opt ∝ C^0.25) extrapolates to ~2800. 2048 lies in the overlap, and the loss curve around the optimum is flat enough that neighbouring widths cost <0.06.\n- **Learning rate**: predicted edge at 2048 ≈ 8.5e-4 (6e-4–1.25e-3 across plausible exponents). eta = 4.5e-4 is ~0.53× nominal edge and ≤0.75× even in the worst case, avoiding both divergence (an 8.0 write-off) and spike damage, at a cost of only ~0.01–0.02 versus a closer-to-edge setting.\n- **Interval** [3.12, 3.52] (width 0.40) brackets the model predictions from the different fits (≈3.20–3.44) with margin for extrapolation error."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":320,"cache_read_input_tokens":44112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":320},"output_tokens":620,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent